From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] busybox: udhcpc crash fix and tar extraction backports
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Keep busybox 1.37.0 (already carrying the 0030 backports) and add:

- A LOCAL (not upstream) fix for CVE-2026-88833: udhcpc's raw-socket
  receive path (networking/udhcp/dhcpc.c:d4_recv_raw_packet()) trusts
  the sender-controlled IP tot_len as the packet length without
  re-checking it against the minimum DHCP header size. A tot_len
  smaller than sizeof(ip)+sizeof(udp) underflows the later
  "bytes -= sizeof(ip)+sizeof(udp)" subtraction and feeds memcpy() a
  ~2^64 length, crashing udhcpc; the same gap lets the RFC1048 magic
  cookie be matched outside the claimed packet length. Checked against
  busybox upstream master (5eee8017a, 2026-10-22), the busybox mailing
  list archive and bug tracker, the CVE record, and OpenWrt main/25.12
  on 2026-10-31: no upstream fix exists yet, so this re-validates the
  minimum size after tot_len is substituted in, mirroring the bound
  upstream commit fd1972099 already applies to the pre-substitution
  length. See REPORT.md for upstream status and test evidence.

- Two October 2026 busybox upstream commits for archival/tar.c and
  archival/libarchive/ tar extraction, backported unmodified:
  5da20102b ("tar: \"..\" is also an unsafe filename, treat as such")
  and 382008b3f ("tar: protect against Symlink+Hardlink attack", with
  the comment-only follow-up 32653c392 folded in). Together they close
  the gap in the CVE-2026-26157/26158 fix (patches 005/006) where a
  deferred symlink/hardlink pair could still place a file outside the
  extraction directory; this is the same issue tracked as
  CVE-2026-108119.

PKG_RELEASE bumped 7 -> 8.
